, which equals -30%. This means that there is a 30% lower percentage of Republicans who agree with the tea party movement compared to Democrats.\n<step-5>\nSo, the correct answer is -30%.\n<think>\n<answer>\n-30%\n</answer>\n</think>'}], [{'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<think>\n<type>\npie\n</type>\n<table>\n{"columns": ["category", "percentage (%)"], "rows": [["Democrat/lean Dem", "47"], ["Rep/lean R Agree with Tea Party", "17"], ["Rep/lean R Disagree or no opinion", "23"], ["No partisan leaning", "13"]]}\n</table>\n<step-1>\nThe chart represents the agreement with the Tea Party Movement among Republicans and Democrats. It is in the form of a pie chart, which visually displays the percentage of each group.\n<step-2>\nFrom the pie chart, the category for Democrats shows "Democrat/lean Dem", with a percentage of 47% agreeing with the Tea Party Movement. The category for Republicans who agree with the Tea Party Movement is "Rep/lean R Agree with Tea Party", which represents 17% of Republicans who agree.\n<step-3>\nTo find the difference in the percentage between Democrats and Republicans on agreeing with the Tea Party Movement, subtract the percentage of Republicans who agree from the percentage of Democrats who agree. \n<step-4>\nThe calculation is as follows: \n\\[ 47\\% \\text{ (Democrats)} - 17\\% \\text{ (Republicans who agree)} = 30\\% \\]\n</step-5>\nThe difference between Democrats and Republicans on agreeing with the Tea Party Movement is 30 percentage points.\n</think>\n<answer>\n30\n</answer>'}]]
